00:00:02.629 --> 00:00:03.830 align:start position:0%
stafford avenue district council is  currently consulting on a site  allocations plan  this video focuses on two specific site  proposals that are closely related to  the town of stratford-upon-avon  both of which are for business uses it  is important to bear in mind that both  sides are already allocated in the core  strategy adopted in july 2016  so the principle of their development is  already established  proposal sua2 is south of ulster road  the site comprises 23 hectares of land  south of the a46 ulster road  immediately to the west of wildsmore  roundabout  the two main purposes behind the site  being allocated are  one to provide an opportunity for  companies to move to the town  in order to bolster the local economy  and provide new jobs  and two to provide scope for businesses  in the canal quarter regeneration zone  to relocate and allow that area to be  redeveloped  however circumstances have changed in  recent years and the district council  believes that a more flexible approach  is justified  regarding the types of business uses  that are appropriate on the site  in particular provision is now made for  a car dealership and a bulky goods  retail store  as well as for offices and industrial  uses  what is retained is the scope for  businesses to relocate from the canal  quarter regeneration zone  specific controls will be applied to  ensure that such businesses have the  opportunity to do so for a period of  time  once the site starts to be developed  it should be noted that outline paneling  permission was granted in december 2019  for a mixed-use business park  associated with this is a full planning  permission for a new roundabout access  from the a46 then we've got proposal  sua4  atherston airfield this site is part of  a former airfield located on the a3  a4 300 ships in road about two  kilometers from the southern edge of the  town  an area of 10 hectares is identified for  employment uses  the original proposal sought to restrict  these uses to businesses relocating from  the canal quarter  again however it is apparent to the  district council that a more flexible  approach is required in order to  implement the site  giving the infrastructure costs involved  for this reason it is proposed that the  relocation of businesses  from elsewhere in the district including  those already based on other parts of  the oscar to state should be supported  in addition this may be extended to  businesses relocating from outside the  district  if it can be justified in order to  facilitate the delivery of the canal  quarter  a detailed transport assessment will be  required to establish the impact of  additional traffic on the local road  network  the provision of extensive landscaping  around the edge of the site to reduce  visual impact on the surrounding area  will be expected  i hope this has helped explain these two  sites and remember you can find out more  about the site allocations plan and  submit any comments you have  by visiting our website at  www.stratford.gov dot uk forward slash  sappo
 

